    "question": "Given our enterprise environment, our products often involve complex workflows and diverse user groups. Could you walk me through your typical approach to understanding user needs and defining a problem space when starting a new UX project in such a setting?",
    "category": "UX Process & User Research",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "expectedTopics": ["user research methods", "problem definition", "stakeholder analysis", "journey mapping", "persona development"]
  },
  {
    "question": "In an enterprise company, collaboration across different teams like engineering, product management, and various business stakeholders is absolutely crucial. How do you typically ensure your design solutions are not only user-centered but also technically feasible and aligned with the broader business objectives?",
    "category": "Collaboration & Design Strategy",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "expectedTopics": ["cross-functional collaboration", "communication skills", "balancing constraints", "stakeholder management", "design iteration"]
  },
  {
    "question": "We often work on products that have a significant impact on many users. Could you describe a time when you had to make a critical design decision with incomplete information or under tight constraints? How did you approach that situation, and how did you measure the success or impact of your decision?",
    "category": "Problem Solving & Design Impact",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "expectedTopics": ["decision-making", "risk mitigation", "iterative design", "metrics and KPIs", "user feedback", "adaptability"]
  }
]
